WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Speaker 1: Welcome back to the show producer Pat&nbsp;
Forde filling in for David today as he continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.360
his paternity leave. So Joe Biden is weighing&nbsp;
whether to set in place a gas tax holiday in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.920
response to the ballooning gas prices, which&nbsp;
have actually come down a little bit in recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.600
days. And I'll get to that in a second. But as&nbsp;
I'm sure many of you know, there's a federal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:24.240
gasoline tax. It's 18.3 cents per gallon. And so&nbsp;
the money goes towards restoring roads and bridges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.120
all across the country. But with prices of&nbsp;
gasoline at around $5 a gallon right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.840
there's this idea floating that maybe it would&nbsp;
be a good idea to provide temporary relief to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.480
Americans who are feeling it at the pump and&nbsp;
suspend the gas tax. The decision is supposed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.040
come from the Joe Biden administration at the end&nbsp;
of the week. However, you really need Congress to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.560
enact this. Biden said that he is also weighing&nbsp;
whether to send Americans gas rebate cards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.120
saying that that's part of what they're&nbsp;
considering and that's part of the operation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.960
Previously, the administration said that&nbsp;
it would be too difficult to put in place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.200
a system for gas rebate cards, but&nbsp;
now they're taking another look at it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.840
When it comes to the gas tax holiday, I get the&nbsp;
sense that if Joe Biden wants it, the Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.680
are going to go along with it and he'll be&nbsp;
able to get the votes, although, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.880
Democrats are often cautious about doing anything&nbsp;
that will do away with, you know, funds for things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.200
like infrastructure. The question is, would&nbsp;
Republicans go along with it, though, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.400
more than they want to actually fix these issues&nbsp;
surrounding inflation and high gas prices and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.520
the like. They want to have something to attack&nbsp;
Joe Biden on. So they're totally happy, in my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.720
opinion, seeing gas prices go up and up and up&nbsp;
because it gives them a greater chance possibly of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.080
winning in the midterms. So maybe they'll oppose&nbsp;
Joe Biden's tax holiday idea and then turn around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.520
and blame him for the high gas prices. The Triple&nbsp;
A national average for a gallon of gasoline right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:52.720
now is down to $4.96, which is still exceptionally&nbsp;
high, but it's down from $5.02 a week or so ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.880
So this could be a sign that we've reached the&nbsp;
peak, could be a sign that gas prices are going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.440
to trickle down from here on, but it's still&nbsp;
too early to say. And then you think, okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.040
if we move towards suspending the federal&nbsp;
gas tax, we're looking at an average of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.760
you know, $4.78 per gallon or so. That does sound&nbsp;
a lot better. But is it going to make a material&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.880
difference for the average American? Because&nbsp;
let's say right now it costs, say, 80 bucks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:23.600
to fill up your tank. Well, now it's going to go&nbsp;
down about $3. It'll be $77 to fill up your tank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.960
which I like. Okay. I get it. For the average&nbsp;
people out there just trying to make ends meet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.600
it could make some difference. Right. But I think&nbsp;
for the most part, this is more about politics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.720
It's more about making it so that Joe Biden looks&nbsp;
like he's trying to actually solve the issue. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:44.000
for some Americans, it just helps sort of at the&nbsp;
psychological level that if you drive by the gas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.880
station, that the numbers are going down a little&nbsp;
bit, that it's now $4.87 instead of $5. That helps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:56.400
a little bit, right? We have the same conversation&nbsp;
whenever we talk about the idea of taking more oil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.960
out of the Strategic Petroleum Reserve, that it&nbsp;
can do some good. Right. But at the end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.280
day, it's only going to save you about $0.10&nbsp;
a gallon, $0.20 a gallon. So is that going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.080
be a substantial difference for most Americans?&nbsp;
And obviously, a big factor in the high price of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:15.680
gas right now isn't just the pandemic recovery&nbsp;
and inflation and Putin's war on Ukraine. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.960
also greed from the oil and gas companies which&nbsp;
are experiencing record profits at the moment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.160
Joe Biden said about this that he's going to be&nbsp;
speaking with the oil and gas CEOs, members of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.520
administration specifically will, so they can get&nbsp;
an explanation as to how they're able to make $35&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.960
billion in the first quarter of the year while&nbsp;
the average American is struggling. So that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.280
the latest on gas prices. They are coming down a&nbsp;
little bit, but they would come down quite a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:47.520
deal more if Joe Biden and the Democrats and the&nbsp;
rest of Congress decide to suspend the gas tax.

